            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0444" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.515/60: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-18T19:00:00-04:00">March 18, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Your 62, March 8, 10 a.m. For McBride. The Treasury and War Departments are
                    in consultation regarding the currency problem and expect to furnish us with a
                    definite reply to your recommendation in the near future. It is probable that
                    your suggestions will in large measure be adopted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
